{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 0916bf3d65cd71b7bfd734d9575da7ac6dcf69be, tree cb5049b255137fbe194d6ff58d072b646570d3fd, on builder/ek1-es1-20261116, all 36 artifacts, for request b86c4bb9 under my promise 566109cb. This verdict names one implementation: promise 7407f3c0, report 2f3957ac (the EK-1 and ES-1 note, primary). `gs review --prepare` bound that promise to request abaa0b9b (ES-1) only, with that request closing on the sealed receipt. It found no binding for request c4856f3a (EK-1) at this head. Main 06afc9d6 is the base, and four commits change 36 paths.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The kernel, `packages/derive`. `checkGrantValue` is the one private value check. It runs the value checks of `judgeGrant` in the same order: whose answer it is, the key, a revocation, then the caller's use guards, then key state, action, `within`, end time and controller. `judgeGrant` passes its old use guards as `between`, unchanged, and still returns `grantFrom(use)`. `judgeExploreGrant` passes no use guard and returns `valueGrant`, which is the seven members with no own `fresh` member. In `judgeActBody`, `hasProof` lets such a value sign the body. `granted` is then null, and a body with rows in `observes` answers `unavailable`. So the value never serves a row or becomes recordable authority. The only new kernel export is `judgeExploreGrant`. `forms-grant.test.ts` pins the bytes of `grantFrom`.\n- The scope. The sessions route accepts exactly one `standing=1`. Any other `standing` gets `400 bad-request` before the body is read. `issueSession` adds the standing value that it already made for the checks and claims, only for `standing === true`. With no option, the route names three members whatever the object returns. `roomApi` passes no second argument when there is no option, so an older object sees the old call.\n- The client. `requestSession` adds the query only for `standing: true`. `isSessionAnswer` admits a fourth member only when it is named `standing`. `sessionStanding` requires exactly the thirteen members, each with its form. It requires a pinned platform membership that answers the session question, `notAfter: null`, and agreement with the request and the claims on membership, key, member and filter. A value that fails leaves the session without a standing. `AUTHORITY_REFUSALS` is `[\"unauthorized\"]`, and the note gives the source for each path to that reason.\n- The CLI. The cache record admits a fifth member, `standing`, and checks it again with `sessionStanding` on load. A submit whose answer is an authority refusal discards the cached session.\n- MCP. `sessionAt` keeps the held session only when its standing head equals the head of the membership read of the same moment. Otherwise it forgets the session and asks once more, as ruling c1fd1293 asks. `standingFrom` asks `judgeExploreGrant` for each action and decides nothing itself. `viewer` and `actions` in `service.ts` use `sessionAt`. `budget.test.ts` pins both costs.\n- The version rule. Only the `presentation` IDs of Lending and Counter change, and both declare the open 0.5.0. No signed release file changes.\n- The seals. `security-entry-points.test.mjs` replaces 11 hashes. Each belongs to a file that this head changes, and the pins stage passed on them. The reasons for `service.ts`, `inventory.ts`, `command-support.ts`, `read-session-cache.ts` and `session.ts` now name C4 and EK-1 or ES-1, which answers point 2 of my review f3e211f3.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 36 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 06afc9d6 0916bf3d`.\n- The gate, END b65c0acd, on this exact head. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-16-ek1-es1-gate/gate.log` names head 0916bf3d and tree cb5049b2 with 0 changed files. Pins passed in 17.6 s. Plain 4985 with 1 skipped and Native 1169 with 2 skipped passed. The crossing counts were lost 0, stale 3 and no-owner 0, and the last line is \"gate passed\". The request explains